From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] e200: fix Charon TAP creation on E200 kernel

Add the libtuntap fix required for the E200 kernel's TUNSETIFF behavior.
---
diff --git a/package/charon/0003-fix-libtuntap-ifname.patch b/package/charon/0003-fix-libtuntap-ifname.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..78dfe82e8a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/charon/0003-fix-libtuntap-ifname.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] libtuntap: retain the name returned by TUNSETIFF
+
+The pinned libtuntap calls SIOCSIFNAME before initializing dev->if_name.
+E200's kernel rejects the rename with ENODEV even though TUNSETIFF has
+already created the requested ofdm0 device.  TUNSETIFF already assigned
+the desired name, so retain it directly.
+
+--- a/third_party/libtuntap/tuntap-unix-linux.c
++++ b/third_party/libtuntap/tuntap-unix-linux.c
+@@ -107,7 +107,9 @@ tuntap_sys_start(struct device *dev, int mode, int tun) {
+ 		return -1;
+ 	}
+ 
+-  tuntap_sys_set_ifname(dev, "ofdm0\0", 6);
++	/* TUNSETIFF already created the requested name.  Do not issue a
++	 * second SIOCSIFNAME using the uninitialized dev->if_name. */
++	(void)memcpy(dev->if_name, ifr.ifr_name, sizeof(dev->if_name));

